@@ -153,6 +153,32 @@ The feed is FIR-wide (one `LLLL` source, ~120 NOTAMs) with no per-chart field, b
 
 **Show NOTAMs is remembered per chart** (`navaid.showNotam.<cvfr|lsa|heli>`): CVFR cross-country can keep the airspace NOTAMs up while an LSA or helicopter chart is flown without them. A chart you have never set **inherits** whatever you chose last, so nothing disappears the first time you switch; the charts diverge only once you actually toggle one. On Satellite / OSM / Navigation the choice follows whatever **Nav waypoints from** is showing.
 
+## Surface weather
+
+**Show surface weather** (Weather) puts the forecast at the surface on the chart, now and for the
+next 48 hours: Open-Meteo, on a 0.25° grid over Israel, in one request when it is switched on. The
+time slider re-samples it without asking again.
+
+- **Points**, one of:
+  - **Station plot: temperature / dew point** (default): the temperature above, the dew point
+    below, and the dot between them coloured by the spread: red at 2 °C or less, amber at 4 °C or
+    less. The dew point takes the dot's colour, so a red pair reads as fog at a glance.
+  - **Dew point spread**: the spread at each point, the number always beside its dot.
+  - **Cloud base (estimate)**: (T − Td) × 400 ft above the ground, the same rule as
+    [Route check](Route-Check).
+  - **No points**.
+- **Isobars (sea-level pressure)**: a switch of their own, drawn under any point style, every
+  2 hPa and labelled. **H** and **L** mark only real centres (the extreme within about 60 km, and
+  at least 1.5 hPa off the ring around it), so a flat day shows none.
+- A chip on the map names what is shown, the hour and the units, and the legend has a line for
+  each part.
+- While it is on, the waypoint [inspector](Inspector) adds a **Surface** row (T / Td, spread,
+  QNH) and **Cloud base (est.)** both above the ground and above sea level, e.g.
+  `1,200 ft AGL · 3,800 ft AMSL`. Above sea level is the figure to compare with an altimeter on
+  QNH, and over the hills it differs most.
+- Off by default (`defaultSurfaceWx`); the gist can withdraw it (`featureSurfaceWx`). It is also
+  in the map's [quick layers](The-Map#quick-layers).
+
 ## Wind effect
 
 Toggle **Show wind effect** to draw per-leg wind arrows, the route-wide wind
