+### On the way back
+
+With **Show return path** on, the way home gets its own callouts: at each change point, the
+station flown *into* coming back, worked out on the route reversed. On LLHA → LLIB, GILAM is
+Pluto East going and Haifa coming back; DESHE is Rosh Pina going and Pluto East coming back.
+
+- They are ordinary callouts: drag, re-tune, reset or delete them. Tapping one opens the waypoint
+  panel marked *On the way back (return path)*. The way out's callout at the same point is never
+  touched.
+- They sit on the way back's side of the track (see
+  [Route and Legs](Route-and-Legs#with-the-return-path-shown)), their text turned to read on a
+  chart turned round. Colour: `commChangeReturnArrowColor` (black, like the way out).
