 ## What you set
 
-Open **📋 Flight plan** and use the **Aircraft** row at the top:
+Choose the **Aircraft type** in **Settings** (C172 by default; C152, C172, PA28, DA40, SR22, AT3,
+C42, EV97, ULAC). It fills the two figures below, the usable fuel the flight plan form uses for
+endurance, and the climb rate and speed the vertical profile uses. They sit in **Custom figures**:
+change any of them and a dot marks it, its tooltip gives the type's value, and **Restore C172
+figures** puts them all back. Leg speed is not part of the aircraft; it keeps its own setting.
+
+The two fuel figures are also in the **Aircraft** row at the top of **📋 Flight plan**:
 
 | Field | Meaning |
 | --- | --- |
-| **Gallons per hour** | Cruise burn. Seeds from the `defaultGph` tuning key on first use. |
-| **Taxi and Takeoff (gal)** | A flat allowance added once, and only when the leg actually starts at an airfield. |
+| **Gallons per hour** | Cruise burn. From the aircraft type (C172: 8.5). |
+| **Taxi and Takeoff (gal)** | A flat allowance added once, and only when the leg actually starts at an airfield. From the aircraft type (C172: 1.1). |
 
 Both persist per device under `navaid.aircraft` (`{ gph, taxiGal }`) and sync across your devices if Drive settings sync is on — see [Settings and Persistence](Settings-and-Persistence).
 
