+## Quick layers
+
+The **Layers** button (stacked sheets) heads the edit column, above Route check. It opens a short
+list beside the column:
+
+- **Chart**: the base maps. Picking one switches the map and closes the list.
+- **Overlays**: switches for NOTAMs, airspace, SIGMET, AIRMET, per-leg wind, airfield charts,
+  traffic and [surface weather](Extra-Layers#surface-weather), each the same switch as in the
+  menu. A switch leaves the list open, so several can be flipped in one visit.
+- A layer this device cannot show (traffic in a browser), or with nothing in force (an idle AIRMET
+  or SIGMET), is dimmed and says why when pressed. Only a layer the gist removed is left out.
+- Escape, a tap outside, Android Back or the button again closes it.
+
+## Airfields up close
+
+Far out, an airfield is its fixed-size symbol. Zoomed in, once its runway would draw longer than
+the symbol, the runway itself is drawn between its true ends. For 13 fields (LLHZ, LLHA, LLER,
+LLBO, LLES, LLEY, LLFK, LLKS, LLKZ, LLMG, LLMZ, LLAR, LLRS) it is laid on the chart's own printed
+runway bar, so it lines up with the CVFR chart. LLBS and LLBG, and the other civil fields, use the
+real runway from OpenStreetMap, which over satellite imagery lies on the tarmac and on the chart
+sits beside the printed bar. Military fields keep their circle.
+
